pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression: the input formula is UNSATISFIABLE (x1 must be both true and
% false). Constraint 2 cannot be derived from constraint 1, so `del id 2`
% falls back to unchecked deletion, and the output formula is then just
% `1 x1 >= 1` -- which IS satisfiable. `output EQUISATISFIABLE` is therefore a
% false claim in the sharpest possible way: unsatisfiable in, satisfiable out.
%
% This is the backward direction of an equivalence failing, and it is the leg
% the kernel's `DbBack` development isolates: `dbBack_append` is
% unconditional, `dbBack_delete_checked` is the ONLY leg carrying an
% obligation, and there is deliberately no unchecked-delete leg because the
% invariant genuinely does not survive one. The live guard is
% `Context::strong_solution_guarantees`, cleared on the fallback in
% `rules/deletion.rs` and required by `rules/output.rs`.
f 2;
del id 2;
output EQUISATISFIABLE FILE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
